ee really um willingness on any part  um to to do that basically it's uh  it's it's negotiations between israel  and  a bunch of gulf arab states they have  a lot of common interest even outside  any  u.s help so they would have  proceeded with these kind of negotiate  negotiations  anyway irrespective of the palestinian  question  briefly could you see other arab states  joining in we have just a couple of  seconds  so yes or no  yeah the odd man out now is saudi arabia  so  the uee has clearly taken the forefront  as the most important  publicly visible ally of the of the  united states  and just one last thing we have to pay  attention to  the main architect of this policy this  is  muhammad bin zayed the crown prince of  abu dhabi probably the most influential  arab politicians in our time  he's stepping out of the shadows step by  step so  keep a close look how he's behaving  robert chatterjee from zenith magazine  here in germany  you
 

